-- title:
--   Special fibre of the Drinfeld blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a discrete valuation ring $O$ (a commutative domain) whose residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField O` is algebraically closed and carries an algebra structure over the field `GaloisField q 2` with $q^2$ elements, and assume that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q` $\kappa$ — the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q` $\kappa$ $- 1$ — is a domain. Let $\pi \in O$ generate the maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in O$ be non-zero and in the maximal ideal, and let `pr` be a chart presentation for $\varpi$: power series $f, u, v \in O[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Put $S = O[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varpi^{q+1}v - fu)$ with quotient map `mkS`, and assume the image of the constant $\varpi$ is a non-zero-divisor in $S$. Let $L$ be the localisation of $S$ away from that image, $\iota_0 : O \to L$ the map induced by constants, $x_0, x_1 \in L$ the images of $X_0, X_1$ divided by $\varpi$, and $R \subseteq L$ the subring generated by the image of $S$ together with $x_0$ and $x_1$. The assertion is that $\iota_0(O) \subseteq R$, that $x_0, x_1 \in R$, and that for the ideal $P = (\iota_0 \pi)$ of $R$: $R$ is Noetherian, $P$ is prime, $R/P$ carries a $\kappa$-algebra structure for which the class of $\iota_0 a$ is the image of $\mathrm{residue}(a)$ for all $a \in O$, and there are a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e_R : R/P \simeq$ `CoordRing q` $\kappa$ and a scalar $c \in \kappa$ such that: every element of $S$ of the form $\mathrm{mkS}(a + X_0g_0 + X_1g_1)$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal of $O$ lies in $R$ and in $P$; $c \neq 0$; $c^{q+1}$ times the residue of the constant coefficient of $u$ equals the residue of the constant coefficient of $v$; and $e_R$ sends the classes of $x_0$ and $x_1$ to $c \cdot$ `x q` $\kappa$ and $c \cdot$ `y q` $\kappa$ respectively.
--
--   This is the special-fibre half of the description of the weighted blow-up chart of a local Drinfeld chart at an arbitrary non-zero parameter $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal: after adjoining $X_0/\varpi$ and $X_1/\varpi$, reduction modulo the uniformiser yields the affine Drinfeld curve over the residue field, up to a common rescaling $c$ of the two coordinates determined by the constant coefficients of $u$ and $v$. It is used by [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_algEquiv_coordRing_and_isDiscreteValuationRing_blowupChart_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_algEquiv_coordRing_and_isDiscreteValuationRing_blowupChart_of_mem_maximalIdeal), which adds the statement that the localisation of $R$ at $P$ is a discrete valuation ring.
